        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ealdgyth, Edith, Sigeferth, Earngrim, Edmund II, Edmund Ironside\n- Roles: wife, son, thegn, King of England\n\nFacts:\n- Ealdgyth, rendered in modern English as Edith, lived circa 992 to after 1016.\n- Ealdgyth may have been the wife of Sigeferth, son of Earngrim.\n- Sigeferth was the son of Earngrim and was a thegn of the Seven Wessex.\n- Ealdgyth later may have been the wife of Edmund II.\n- Edmund II, usually known as Edmund Ironside, was King of England from 23 April 1016 to 30 November 1016.",
